    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name DeBordieu has French roots meaning coastal border or edge of water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeBordieu_Colony%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Marquis de Lafayette landed his ship here in 1777 and exclaimed that the land must be the borderland of God.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.debordieucolony.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Local Gullah dialect influenced the southern pronunciation of DeBordieu Colony as Debidue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.debordieucolony.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "DeBordieu Colony is one of the oldest beachside communities on the East Coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.debordieucolony.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Roughly 800 acres of the 2,700 acres in DeBordieu Colony are preserved as an inaccessible wildlife preserve.",
